<p>President Trump said Wednesday that the United States is studying a possible reduction of American troops in Germany and would decide within a short period, after a public dispute with German Chancellor Friedrich Merz over the war in Iran. Germany hosts the largest U.S. military presence in Europe; the articles give figures ranging from more than 35,000 troops in 2024 to about 38,000 U.S. troops and personnel and about 39,000 soldiers in mid-April. The announcement followed Merz&#x27;s remarks Monday that Iran&#x27;s leadership was humiliating Washington and that the Trump administration lacked a convincing strategy to end the war. Trump responded sharply on Truth Social. Trump has also criticized some NATO allies for not supporting the U.S.-Israeli war against Iran and for not sending naval forces to help reopen the Strait of Hormuz.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/OA3EVnhHoAKoZoDCA2zMj85USaB0jYe_TQ6IDVIaSFZEKvYsxxZ6FCkFkizOJJhyh7-NxLU27spmbhDKGFo-7J3NPIkiOdKIVM5lU732myMbgLzir_rYHZ-IglmvSgeGklgHUJDkjYpHFBgBnnw' alt='U.S. Army soldiers and an M109A7 Paladin self-propelled howitzer take part in a live-fire exercise in Germany.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Congress: Politico reported that any reduction in the Germany-based force would face opposition on Capitol Hill because the deployment has strong congressional support.</li><li>Defense spending: Pentagon officials recently described Germany as a model NATO ally, citing Berlin&#x27;s plan to raise defense spending to 3.7% of GDP by 2030.</li><li>Regional bases: Romania and Poland have welcomed larger U.S. deployments, but Politico reported that Germany hosts U.S. European Command and that few large alternative sites are available, complicating any major shift.</li><li>Diplomatic contact: U.S. Secretary of State Marco Rubio spoke by phone with German Foreign Minister Johann Wadephul about Iran and freedom of navigation in the Strait of Hormuz before Trump&#x27;s post on the troop review.</li></ul><blockquote>The United States is studying and reviewing the possible reduction of Troops in Germany, with a determination to be made over the next short period of time - President Donald Trump</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>President Donald Trump: After Merz&#x27;s comments on Iran, Trump wrote that the German chancellor did not know what he was talking about and tied the dispute to Germany&#x27;s economic situation. (<a href='https://www.rt.com/news/639286-trump-germany-troops-merz/'>RT</a>)</li><li>German Chancellor Friedrich Merz: Merz later played down any personal rift, saying his relationship with Trump remained as good as before. (<a href='https://jornaldebrasilia.com.br/noticias/mundo/trump-diz-que-cogita-reduzir-numero-de-tropas-americanas-na-alemanha/'>Jornal de Brasília</a>)</li><li>White House: The White House offered no additional comment on Trump&#x27;s Truth Social statement about the possible troop reduction. (<a href='https://www.politico.com/news/2026/04/29/trump-us-reducing-troops-germany-00899352'>Politico</a>)</li><li>NATO: NATO did not immediately respond to Politico&#x27;s request for comment after Trump said the United States was reviewing its force presence in Germany. (<a href='https://www.politico.com/news/2026/04/29/trump-us-reducing-troops-germany-00899352'>Politico</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/news/639286-trump-germany-troops-merz/'>Trump threatens to pull troops from Germany amid feud with Merz</a> - rt.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/30/trump-threatens-to-reduce-troop-numbers-in-germany-amid-growing-row-with-nato-allies'>Trump threatens to reduce troop numbers in Germany amid growing row with Nato allies</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/trump-threatens-us-troop-cuts-in-germany/a-76987910'>Trump threatens US troop cuts in Germany</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/trump-possible-reduction-us-troops-germany/'